% global_cardinality with CONSTANT counts: a refutation the constants DRIVE, and one
% that needs SEARCH to reach (M7-T18, D-0082).
%
% One 1, one 2, two 3s over x1..x4, with x1 + x2 <= 4 and x3 + x4 <= 4. A 3 can only
% sit beside a 1, so the two 3s need two 1s if they are in different pairs, and sum to 6
% if they are in the same one. UNSAT, and nothing prunes at the root: neither linear row
% excludes a value on its own, and gcc's capacities are not yet tight. Every branch is
% closed by the constant counts -- rule A's capacity push (the 1 is used up) feeding a
% linear row, or rule C's shortfall on the 3s -- so the refutation rests on the
% constants throughout.
%
% D-0066: `rup` lines over an UNSAT model can be vacuous, so this lane is the
% refutation's half; the pruning half over a satisfiable model is gcc_const_counts_sat.
var 1..3: x1;
var 1..3: x2;
var 1..3: x3;
var 1..3: x4;
constraint int_lin_le([1,1],[x1,x2],4);
constraint int_lin_le([1,1],[x3,x4],4);
constraint fzn_global_cardinality([x1,x2,x3,x4],[1,2,3],[1,1,2]);
solve :: int_search([x1,x2,x3,x4], input_order, indomain_min, complete) satisfy;
